-- zui.stzu -- StzZui, declared as a Haro language
--
-- The first artifact of the re-declaration ruled on 2026-10-31. Written FROM the pack's own
-- data (conformance/media.json, signal.json, violations.json, doc/language/DECLARATIONS.md)
-- and judged by the stzu meta-court:
--     rnxc haro.ring zui.stzu       (ringpp/haro/spike)
-- The verifier (tools/zui/zui.js) is NOT changed and NOT replaced by this file. This file
-- declares what the meta-language can carry; the SEAMS below count what it cannot.
--
-- Words are lower_snake here and UPPER in a .zui file (DISCOVER, SATISFIES): the meta-language
-- reserves UPPER_SNAKE for its own keywords, and Z made the same trade ("a step is lower_snake
-- here where ZQL names it UPPER"). Case is the forge's printer to restore, not a declaration.
--
-- SEAMS -- what the stzu of 2026-10-31 cannot carry, counted against violations.json (33):
--   S1  severity: every refusal a court speaks is an error. Five diagnostics are warnings in
--       zui.js (UNSPECIFIED_DECLARATION, INTENT_FLOW_NO_SATISFIES, UNRESOLVED_INTENT_FLOW,
--       UNRESOLVED_ENTITY, ROLE_UNDECLARED) and are NOT declared here, so the court does not
--       over-refuse. The exception is WIDGET and USER, see D2.
--   S2  cites: CONSTRAINT carries CODE and no CITES, so a refusal cites rule:<element name>
--       and not rule:16 / article:intent / pattern:select-silently-acts. REFUSAL and SYMBOL
--       have CITES; CONSTRAINT, MENU, RANGE, FORMAT and UNION do not.
--   S3  the world: INTENT_ORPHAN, INVISIBLE_STATE, HIDDEN_AUTHORITY check a host world in the
--       direction "everything the world holds is declared", which SYMBOL (a declared name
--       resolves) does not say. Level 3 is not carried.
--   S4  the rendered surface: LAYOUT_DISPLACEMENT (level 4) is judged on a pixel, not a
--       declaration. It stays with the tool tier of the enforcement ladder.
--   S5  a universal field: SATISFIES, ALWAYS_REACHABLE, SIGNALS and ACTOR belong to every
--       kind and the meta-language has no "on every declaration", so they repeat on all ten.
--   S6  the media matrix: 77 cells are "absent" in media.json; two are carried below as the
--       proof that a cross-declaration cell can be said (zoom on auditory and voice). The
--       other 75 are sayable the same way and are the forge's to generate, not hand-written.
--   S7  VIBE_STRIPS_RIGHT needs "a suppressed verb that ANY declaration guarantees": a join of
--       the values of one list against the lists of other declarations. I found no such form in the
--       condition language of 2026-10-31; that is not a proof that none can be made.
--   S8  ROLE_MISPLACED: a seat that exists on one kind only is, elsewhere, an unknown clause
--       and refuses as PARSE; the code and the sentence "a role belongs to an INTERACTION"
--       are lost.
--   S9  the multi-pillar file: zui.js ignores other pillars' declarations silently; a
--       declared language refuses what it does not know. Ruling needed (D3).
--   S10 RATIONALE: the Commons (stzu GRAMMAR, C6 3.8) makes RATIONALE mandatory on every
--       declaration of a language the forge makes; a .zui declaration has none. Adopting the
--       court means every .zui declaration says why. That is a language change, not a
--       translation. RULED 2026-10-31: .zui 1.3 gains no mandatory RATIONALE (D4); at the
--       boundary a declaration with none reaches the court as "none given".
--   S11 codes: DUPLICATE_FIELD is refused as PARSE, DUPLICATE_DECLARATION as DUPLICATE_NAME and
--       FIELD_MISPLACED as UNKNOWN_CLAUSE. All are refused; the codes StzZui published are not
--       the ones spoken.
--   S12 first refusal: the forged court's diagnose speaks the first refusal it meets;
--       zui.js reports every one. The collecting court exists (haro.ring all) and is not
--       what a forged court does yet.
--
-- DIVERGENCES from zui.js that this declaration makes by being closed (each is a ruling for
-- the author, not a decision taken here):
--   D1  CLOSED at language v1.4 (2026-11-01). Fields are declared per kind from DECLARATIONS.md;
--       zui.js used to accept any field on any kind and ignore a misplaced TONE or PERSPECTIVE
--       silently. It now refuses it as FIELD_MISPLACED (ROLE stays ROLE_MISPLACED), so court and
--       verifier agree on which placements are refused; only the code spoken differs (S11).
--   D2  WIDGET and USER are named and refused as errors; zui.js reports them as a warning.
--       RULED 2026-10-31: the verifier keeps its warning, until Haro has a severity seat.
--   D3  other pillars' kinds are refused, not ignored (S9). RULED 2026-10-31: the verifier ignores.
--   D4  every declaration gains a RATIONALE (S10). RULED 2026-10-31: .zui 1.3 is unchanged and the
--       translator writes "none given"; RATIONALE stays mandatory in the agent's grammar.
--
-- MEASURED 2026-11-01 by haro/judge-zui-court.js: the 52 fixtures of conformance/manifest.json, each
-- translated mechanically into the Commons shape (AS, lower_snake words, RATIONALE "none given") and
-- judged by the court forged from this file. 39 agree with the manifest (20 of them lawful twins
-- judged clean). 13 differ, and each is a named seam: 4 are warnings not declared (S1), 3 need the host
-- world (S3), 3 are refused under another code (S11), and one each is VIBE_STRIPS_RIGHT (S7),
-- VERB_NOT_CARRIED on print x ACT (S6) and a foreign pillar refused (S9).

DEFINE LANGUAGE zui AS (
  VERSION "1.4", GRAMMAR "1.4",
  COURT "conformance/manifest.json",
  EXTENSION ".zui"
) RATIONALE "What a human is DOING, declared before anything is rendered: ten declaration kinds over twenty-two intent verbs, judged by a constitution -- the surface is a consequence and is never named"

-- ---- the closed vocabularies -----------------------------------------------------------

DEFINE MENU intents AS (
  WORDS [discover, understand, locate, focus, filter, compare, read, scan, scroll, zoom, select, highlight, preview, mark, act, confirm, cancel, undo, pause, resume, retry, exit],
  MESSAGE "An intent is one of the twenty-two verbs: DISCOVER, UNDERSTAND, LOCATE, FOCUS, FILTER, COMPARE, READ, SCAN, SCROLL, ZOOM, SELECT, HIGHLIGHT, PREVIEW, MARK, ACT, CONFIRM, CANCEL, UNDO, PAUSE, RESUME, RETRY, EXIT -- the verb set is closed, and NAVIGATE is LOCATE or DISCOVER",
  CODE "UNKNOWN_INTENT"
) RATIONALE "Six families: orienting (discover understand locate), attention (focus filter compare), information (read scan scroll zoom), selection (select highlight preview mark), action (act confirm cancel undo), continuity (pause resume retry exit). The families carry the invariants; a menu has no seat for a family"

DEFINE MENU media AS (
  WORDS [visual, auditory, voice, haptic, print, luminous, signage, machine, spatial, terminal],
  MESSAGE "A surface is projected to one of ten media: visual, auditory, voice, haptic, print, luminous, signage, machine, spatial, terminal -- a kiosk is a visual surface that happens to be unelected, which is a property and not a channel",
  CODE "UNKNOWN_MEDIUM"
) RATIONALE "Closed so that a coverage matrix over media is finite and checkable; a new channel is classified by its six properties, not argued about"

DEFINE MENU signals AS (
  WORDS [success, warning, danger, info, muted],
  MESSAGE "A signal is what a value means about a record: success, warning, danger, info, muted -- a meaning, never a colour",
  CODE "UNKNOWN_SIGNAL"
) RATIONALE "Rule 118 family one; TONE is a different vocabulary and each refuses the other's words"

DEFINE MENU roles AS (
  WORDS [inert, navigate, reversible, irreversible, proposal],
  MESSAGE "A role is the promise a control makes: inert, navigate, reversible, irreversible, proposal",
  CODE "UNKNOWN_ROLE"
) RATIONALE "The consequence of acting, in five values; irreversible is Rule 79's escape clause, or declares why it cannot"

DEFINE MENU tones AS (
  WORDS [celebratory, cautionary, critical, neutral, informational],
  MESSAGE "A tone is the register the system speaks in: celebratory, cautionary, critical, neutral, informational",
  CODE "INVALID_TONE"
) RATIONALE "The MESSAGE stratum; deliberately a separate vocabulary from signals"

DEFINE MENU perspectives AS (
  WORDS [top_down, isometric, first_person, side_scroll],
  MESSAGE "A perspective is top_down, isometric, first_person, side_scroll -- the vantage of a spatial surface",
  CODE "INVALID_PERSPECTIVE"
) RATIONALE "WORLD_VIEW only"

-- ---- the forms and the world -----------------------------------------------------------

DEFINE FORM step AS (
  SEATS [value: name]
) RATIONALE "One named step of a wizard; a list of names is a list of this form written as bare words"

DEFINE FORM state AS (
  SEATS [value: name]
) RATIONALE "One piece of state a navigation shows; a list of names is a list of this form written as bare words"

DEFINE FORM report AS (
  SEATS [value: name]
) RATIONALE "One piece of state a feedback or a moving vibe reports; a list of names is a list of this form written as bare words"

DEFINE FORM entity AS (
  SEATS [value: name]
) RATIONALE "One entity a world view shows; the host world resolves it, and in zui.js an unresolved one is a warning (S1, S3); a list of names is a list of this form written as bare words"


-- ---- the ten kinds ---------------------------------------------------------------------

DEFINE DECLARATION intent_flow AS (
  VERB "INTENT_FLOW",
  SEATS [satisfies: [intents]?, always_reachable: [intents]?, signals: [signals]?, actor: name?]
) RATIONALE "The unit of intent: a named sequence of intents a human moves through; the one kind meant to carry SATISFIES"

DEFINE DECLARATION form AS (
  VERB "FORM",
  SEATS [satisfies: [intents]?, always_reachable: [intents]?, signals: [signals]?, actor: name?, intent_flow: name?]
) RATIONALE "An input surface, bound to a flow rather than restating it"

DEFINE DECLARATION wizard AS (
  VERB "WIZARD",
  SEATS [satisfies: [intents]?, always_reachable: [intents]?, signals: [signals]?, actor: name?, steps: [step]?]
) RATIONALE "A multi-step flow; because it is multi-step, EXIT is always reachable or it is a trap"

DEFINE DECLARATION screen AS (
  VERB "SCREEN",
  SEATS [satisfies: [intents]?, always_reachable: [intents]?, signals: [signals]?, actor: name?]
) RATIONALE "An addressable surface; SATISFIES says why the human came"

DEFINE DECLARATION component AS (
  VERB "COMPONENT",
  SEATS [satisfies: [intents]?, always_reachable: [intents]?, signals: [signals]?, actor: name?]
) RATIONALE "A reusable semantic unit; a component declares meaning, never appearance"

DEFINE DECLARATION nav_graph AS (
  VERB "NAV_GRAPH",
  SEATS [satisfies: [intents]?, always_reachable: [intents]?, signals: [signals]?, actor: name?, visible_state: [state]?]
) RATIONALE "How surfaces connect"

DEFINE DECLARATION world_view AS (
  VERB "WORLD_VIEW",
  SEATS [satisfies: [intents]?, always_reachable: [intents]?, signals: [signals]?, actor: name?, perspective: perspectives?, visible_entities: [entity]?]
) RATIONALE "A spatial surface: a dashboard or a game world seen from a stated vantage"

DEFINE DECLARATION interaction AS (
  VERB "INTERACTION",
  SEATS [satisfies: [intents]?, always_reachable: [intents]?, signals: [signals]?, actor: name?, role: roles?]
) RATIONALE "An act bound to an object, and the host of ROLE because it is the only kind meaning a control's referent without naming a widget"

DEFINE DECLARATION feedback AS (
  VERB "FEEDBACK",
  SEATS [satisfies: [intents]?, always_reachable: [intents]?, signals: [signals]?, actor: name?, tone: tones?, reports: [report]?, motion: name?]
) RATIONALE "What the system says back; feedback that reports nothing is decoration"

DEFINE DECLARATION vibe AS (
  VERB "VIBE",
  SEATS [satisfies: [intents]?, always_reachable: [intents]?, signals: [signals]?, actor: name?, density: name?, surface_as: media?, motion: name?, reports: [report]?, suppresses: [intents]?]
) RATIONALE "An interaction culture: Article VI made declarable. It may set density, motion and surface and may never remove an intent another declaration guarantees"

-- ---- the court: level 2, local semantics ------------------------------------------------
-- Each constraint states the OFFENCE as its WHEN and speaks the diagnostic id as its CODE.
-- CODE is the C2 stable identifier; a cite is not declarable here (S2).

DEFINE CONSTRAINT select_act_collapse_intent_flow AS (
  ON intent_flow, WHEN "satisfies contains select and satisfies contains act and not satisfies contains confirm",
  MESSAGE "{name} selects and acts and never confirms: selection expresses interest, never commitment",
  CODE "SELECT_ACT_COLLAPSE"
) RATIONALE "Rule 16; level 2"

DEFINE CONSTRAINT select_act_collapse_form AS (
  ON form, WHEN "satisfies contains select and satisfies contains act and not satisfies contains confirm",
  MESSAGE "{name} selects and acts and never confirms: selection expresses interest, never commitment",
  CODE "SELECT_ACT_COLLAPSE"
) RATIONALE "Rule 16; level 2"

DEFINE CONSTRAINT select_act_collapse_wizard AS (
  ON wizard, WHEN "satisfies contains select and satisfies contains act and not satisfies contains confirm",
  MESSAGE "{name} selects and acts and never confirms: selection expresses interest, never commitment",
  CODE "SELECT_ACT_COLLAPSE"
) RATIONALE "Rule 16; level 2"

DEFINE CONSTRAINT select_act_collapse_screen AS (
  ON screen, WHEN "satisfies contains select and satisfies contains act and not satisfies contains confirm",
  MESSAGE "{name} selects and acts and never confirms: selection expresses interest, never commitment",
  CODE "SELECT_ACT_COLLAPSE"
) RATIONALE "Rule 16; level 2"

DEFINE CONSTRAINT select_act_collapse_component AS (
  ON component, WHEN "satisfies contains select and satisfies contains act and not satisfies contains confirm",
  MESSAGE "{name} selects and acts and never confirms: selection expresses interest, never commitment",
  CODE "SELECT_ACT_COLLAPSE"
) RATIONALE "Rule 16; level 2"

